  "reviewGuideQuestionsTitle": "Daily questions",
  "@reviewGuideQuestionsTitle": {
    "description": "Title of the step of How reviewing works about the daily questions (docs/REVIEWING.md says the same)."
  },
  "reviewGuideQuestionsBody": "Besides whole decks, you can answer a few short questions a day. The app writes them from the cards, about the data nobody has checked yet: is this the right meaning of a word, is this example natural, is this a real confusable, is this recording correct and by a native speaker.",
  "@reviewGuideQuestionsBody": {
    "description": "First paragraph of the daily questions step of How reviewing works (docs/REVIEWING.md says the same)."
  },
  "reviewGuideQuestionsSend": "Answers wait on your phone until you send them. They go in the same mail as your reviews that wait: tap Send answers here, or send from Settings under Reviewing, and one mail carries everything, a file for each deck and for each language. A data point is settled when two reviewers agree. When one says a point is wrong, that opens a proposal, and the next reviewer decides it: the same answer merges it, a Yes closes it for good. A recording can only be flagged when it is bad, and the card then uses text-to-speech.",
  "@reviewGuideQuestionsSend": {
    "description": "Second paragraph of the daily questions step of How reviewing works (docs/REVIEWING.md says the same). “Send answers” must match reviewQuestionsSend."
  },
  "reviewGuideQuestionsCount": "How many a day is up to you. Pick it here and change it any time in Settings under Reviewing. What you do not answer waits for the next day.",
  "@reviewGuideQuestionsCount": {
    "description": "Third paragraph of the daily questions step of How reviewing works, above the choice of how many a day (docs/REVIEWING.md says the same)."
  },
